        "body": "Define and implement a scalable collection model that can handle thousands or millions of subscribers, repositories, nodes, enrollments, and historical tasks without loading or rendering the entire collection at once.",
        "status": "done",
        "priority": "high",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "nextAction": "",
        "progressNote": "Graph Organization audit found that archive partitions, promotion, portals, summaries, and long-list UI virtualization already exist. The unresolved scaling boundary is earlier in the pipeline: collection graphs still materialize their complete .node membership before the UI can browse them.",
        "blockedReason": "",
        "health": "on-track",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "Collection views can page, filter, sort, and search without materializing every member as a node at once.",
          "The source of truth is separated from bounded visual projections and cached indexes.",
          "Enrollment and policy reconciliation can run incrementally and resume safely.",
          "Completed or inactive members can be archived without breaking durable references or historical provenance."
        ],
        "completedAt": "2026-08-03T21:30:00.000Z",
